    <fr:title text="Monadicity and comonadicity">Monadicity and comonadicity</fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>An adjunction <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F \dashv  U]]></fr:tex> with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F : \mathcal {C} \to  \mathcal {D}]]></fr:tex> and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U : \mathcal {D} \to  \mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> induces a monad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T = U \circ  F]]></fr:tex> on
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>, and a <fr:link href="/sss-00GD/" title="The comparison functor of an adjunction" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00GD/" display-uri="sss-00GD" type="local">comparison functor</fr:link>
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[K : \mathcal {D} \to  \mathrm {EM}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>
sending each object of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {D}]]></fr:tex> to the <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T]]></fr:tex>-algebra it carries.</html:p>
    <html:p>The functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U]]></fr:tex> is <html:em>monadic</html:em> when <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[K]]></fr:tex> is an equivalence: the
adjunction exhibits <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {D}]]></fr:tex> as objects of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> equipped with
algebraic structure for <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T]]></fr:tex>, the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FB/" title="The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FB/" display-uri="sss-00FB" type="local">Eilenberg–Moore category</fr:link>.</html:p>
    <html:p><html:em>Comonadicity</html:em> is monadicity in the opposite category: a left
adjoint <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[L : \mathcal {D} \to  \mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> with right adjoint <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[R]]></fr:tex> induces a
comonad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W = L \circ  R]]></fr:tex> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>, a comparison
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {D} \to  \mathrm {coEM}{\mathopen {}\left (W\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> into the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FC/" title="The co-Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FC/" display-uri="sss-00FC" type="local">co-Eilenberg–Moore category</fr:link>, and <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[L]]></fr:tex> is comonadic when
this comparison is an equivalence.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
