            <fr:display-uri>sss-00FE</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/sss-00FE/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="Presheaves are monadic and comonadic over families">Presheaves are monadic and comonadic over families</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Theorem</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>The <fr:link href="/sss-00FD/" title="The adjoint triple between presheaves and families" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FD/" display-uri="sss-00FD" type="local">adjoint triple</fr:link>
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {Free} \dashv  U \dashv  \mathrm {Cofree}]]></fr:tex> induces a monad
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T = U \circ  \mathrm {Free}]]></fr:tex> and a comonad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W = U \circ  \mathrm {Cofree}]]></fr:tex> on
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {Fam}{\mathopen {}\left (\mathcal {C}\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
            <html:p>Both <fr:link href="/sss-00GD/" title="The comparison functor of an adjunction" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00GD/" display-uri="sss-00GD" type="local">comparison functors</fr:link> are equivalences: presheaves are the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FB/" title="The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FB/" display-uri="sss-00FB" type="local">Eilenberg–Moore algebras</fr:link> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T]]></fr:tex> and the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FC/" title="The co-Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FC/" display-uri="sss-00FC" type="local">co-Eilenberg–Moore coalgebras</fr:link> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex>,
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\mathsf {Psh}\,\mathcal {C} \simeq  \mathrm {EM}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}}
   \qquad 
   \mathsf {Psh}\,\mathcal {C} \simeq  \mathrm {coEM}{\mathopen {}\left (W\right )\mathclose {}}.]]></fr:tex>
So presheaves are both <fr:link href="/sss-00FF/" title="Monadicity and comonadicity" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FF/" display-uri="sss-00FF" type="local">monadic and comonadic</fr:link> over
families.</html:p>
            <html:p>Reading the algebra structure concretely: a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T]]></fr:tex>-algebra on a family
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A]]></fr:tex> is a map <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\sum _{y} \mathcal {C} {\mathopen {}\left (x , y\right )\mathclose {}} \times  A{\mathopen {}\left (y\right )\mathclose {}} \to  A{\mathopen {}\left (x\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>
for each <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x]]></fr:tex>, subject to the monad algebra laws — that is, exactly a
functorial action of restriction.</html:p>
            <html:p>The comonadic reading is the same structure seen from the element's
side: a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex>-coalgebra is a map
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[A{\mathopen {}\left (x\right )\mathclose {}} \to  \prod _{y} \mathcal {C} {\mathopen {}\left (y , x\right )\mathclose {}} \to  A{\mathopen {}\left (y\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>, giving each
value its restriction along every morphism into <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[x]]></fr:tex>. Where the monad
says restriction <html:em>acts on</html:em> values, the comonad says a value
<html:em>already carries</html:em> all of its restrictions — and the coalgebra laws
say it does so coherently.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
