        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
              <fr:author>
                <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
              </fr:author>
            </fr:authors>
            <fr:date>
              <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
              <fr:month>7</fr:month>
              <fr:day>19</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00GD/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sss-00GD</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/sss-00GD/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The comparison functor of an adjunction">The comparison functor of an adjunction</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>An adjunction <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F \dashv  U]]></fr:tex> with <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F : \mathcal {C} \to  \mathcal {D}]]></fr:tex> and
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U : \mathcal {D} \to  \mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> induces a monad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T = U \circ  F]]></fr:tex> on
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>. Write <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\varepsilon  : F \circ  U \Rightarrow  \mathsf {Id}]]></fr:tex> for
the <html:em>counit</html:em> of the adjunction. Every object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[d]]></fr:tex> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {D}]]></fr:tex> then induces
a <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[T]]></fr:tex>-algebra carried by the object <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[U d]]></fr:tex>, witnessed by the map
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[U \varepsilon _{d} : U F U d \to  U d.]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p>This assignment extends to a functor into the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FB/" title="The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FB/" display-uri="sss-00FB" type="local">Eilenberg–Moore category</fr:link>,
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[K : \mathcal {D} \to  \mathrm {EM}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}},]]></fr:tex>
the <html:em>comparison functor</html:em> of the adjunction.</html:p>
            <html:p>Dually, an adjunction induces a comonad on the other side and a
comparison into the <fr:link href="/sss-00FC/" title="The co-Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FC/" display-uri="sss-00FC" type="local">co-Eilenberg–Moore category</fr:link>. When
these comparisons are equivalences we say that the adjunction
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F \dashv  U]]></fr:tex> is <fr:link href="/sss-00FF/" title="Monadicity and comonadicity" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FF/" display-uri="sss-00FF" type="local">(co)monadic</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
              <fr:author>
                <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
              </fr:author>
            </fr:authors>
            <fr:date>
              <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
              <fr:month>7</fr:month>
              <fr:day>19</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FC/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sss-00FC</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/sss-00FC/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The co-Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category">The co-Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>A comonad on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex> <html:em>is</html:em> a monad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}^{\mathrm {op}}]]></fr:tex>.
Everything about its coalgebras is then inherited from the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FB/" title="The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FB/" display-uri="sss-00FB" type="local">Eilenberg–Moore construction</fr:link>, instantiated at the opposite
category — nothing is defined twice.</html:p>
            <html:p>Algebras of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex> over <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}^{\mathrm {op}}]]></fr:tex> are
<fr:link href="/sss-00F9/" title="Coalgebras as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00F9/" display-uri="sss-00F9" type="local">coalgebras</fr:link> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\gamma  \in  \mathcal {C} {\mathopen {}\left (x , W x\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> of the underlying
endofunctor, and the monad algebra laws, read in <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}^{\mathrm {op}}]]></fr:tex>, are the
comonad coalgebra laws — the unit and multiplication of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[W]]></fr:tex>, viewed in
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>, are the counit <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\varepsilon ]]></fr:tex> and comultiplication <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\delta ]]></fr:tex>:
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\gamma  \star  \varepsilon _{x} = \mathsf {id}_{x}
   \qquad 
   \gamma  \star  \delta _{x} = \gamma  \star  W \gamma .]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p>The co-Eilenberg–Moore category is the opposite of the total
category:
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\mathrm {coEM}{\mathopen {}\left (W\right )\mathclose {}} = {\mathopen {}\left (\mathrm {EM}{\mathopen {}\left (W\right )\mathclose {}}\right )\mathclose {}}^{\mathrm {op}}.]]></fr:tex></html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors>
              <fr:author>
                <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
              </fr:author>
            </fr:authors>
            <fr:date>
              <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
              <fr:month>7</fr:month>
              <fr:day>19</fr:day>
            </fr:date>
            <fr:uri>https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FB/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>sss-00FB</fr:display-uri>
            <fr:route>/sss-00FB/</fr:route>
            <fr:title text="The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category">The Eilenberg–Moore category as a displayed category</fr:title>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Fix a monad <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[{\mathopen {}\left (T, \eta , \mu \right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathcal {C}]]></fr:tex>. Its Eilenberg–Moore
category arises in two displayed layers. The first layer is the
<fr:link href="/sss-00F7/" title="Algebras as a displayed category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00F7/" display-uri="sss-00F7" type="local">displayed category of algebras</fr:link> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {AlgStr}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> of the
underlying endofunctor.</html:p>
            <html:p>The second layer, <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {EMStr}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>, is displayed over the
<fr:link href="/sss-00FI/" title="Total category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-00FI/" display-uri="sss-00FI" type="local">total category</fr:link> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathrm {Alg}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>. Over an algebra <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[{\mathopen {}\left (x, \alpha \right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> the displayed
objects are the <html:em>propositions</html:em> that <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\alpha ]]></fr:tex> satisfies the monad
algebra laws:
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\eta _{x} \star  \alpha  = \mathsf {id}_{x}
   \qquad 
   \mu _{x} \star  \alpha  = T \alpha  \star  \alpha .]]></fr:tex></html:p>
            <html:p>The Eilenberg–Moore category is the total category of the tower:
<fr:tex display="block"><![CDATA[\mathrm {EM}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}} = \int  \mathrm {EMStr}{\mathopen {}\left (T\right )\mathclose {}}.]]></fr:tex></html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
